Lab 20: Managing Users and Roles in RHVM
Objectives
By the end of this lab, students will be able to:

Understand the fundamentals of Role-Based Access Control (RBAC) in Red Hat Virtualization Manager (RHVM)
Create and manage user accounts in RHVM environment
Configure and assign different roles to users based on organizational requirements
Implement resource-specific access controls for virtual machines, data centers, and clusters
Test and validate user access permissions across different RHVM components
Troubleshoot common RBAC configuration issues in virtualization environments
Prerequisites
Before starting this lab, students should have:

Basic understanding of Linux system administration
Familiarity with virtualization concepts and terminology
Knowledge of Red Hat Enterprise Linux command-line interface
Understanding of user management principles in enterprise environments
Completed previous RHVM labs covering basic installation and configuration
Access to RHVM web administration portal with administrative privileges
