Task 1: Create New Users and Assign Roles in RHVM
Subtask 1.1: Access RHVM Administration Portal
Open your web browser and navigate to the RHVM administration portal
Log in using the administrator credentials provided in your lab environment
# Default RHVM portal URL format
https://rhvm-manager.example.com/ovirt-engine/
Verify you have administrative access by checking the Administration menu is available
Navigate to Administration → Users to view the current user list
Subtask 1.2: Configure External Authentication (Optional)
If using external authentication sources like LDAP or Active Directory:

Navigate to Administration → Configure
Select Authentication tab
Add authentication domain configuration:
# Example LDAP configuration command
engine-manage-domains add --domain=example.com --provider=ad --user=admin@example.com
Subtask 1.3: Create Internal Users
In the Users tab, click Add to create a new internal user

Fill in the user details:

User Name: vm_operator_01
First Name: Virtual Machine
Last Name: Operator
Email: vm.operator@example.com
Password: Create a secure password
Click OK to save the user

Repeat the process to create additional users:

User Name: storage_admin_01
User Name: network_admin_01
User Name: readonly_user_01
Subtask 1.4: Understanding RHVM Built-in Roles
RHVM provides several built-in roles with different permission levels:

SuperUser: Complete administrative access
ClusterAdmin: Full access to specific clusters
DataCenterAdmin: Full access to specific data centers
HostAdmin: Host management permissions
StorageAdmin: Storage domain management
NetworkAdmin: Network management permissions
VmAdmin: Virtual machine administrative access
UserVmManager: Limited VM management for specific VMs
PowerUserRole: Create and manage own VMs
UserRole: Basic user access to assigned resources
Subtask 1.5: Assign Roles to Users
Select the user vm_operator_01 from the users list

Click Permissions tab in the bottom panel

Click Add to assign permissions

In the Add Permission dialog:

Search: Select Virtual Machines
Object: Choose specific VMs or leave blank for all
Role: Select UserVmManager
User: Confirm vm_operator_01 is selected
Click OK to apply the permission

Assign additional roles:

storage_admin_01: StorageAdmin role for storage domains
network_admin_01: NetworkAdmin role for network resources
readonly_user_01: UserRole for read-only access
Task 2: Configure Role-Based Access to Specific Resources
Subtask 2.1: Create Resource-Specific Permissions
Navigate to Compute → Virtual Machines
Select a specific virtual machine
Click Permissions tab
Add granular permissions:
# Example: Assign VM-specific permissions
User: vm_operator_01
Role: UserVmManager
Object: Specific VM (TestVM-01)
Subtask 2.2: Configure Cluster-Level Access
Navigate to Compute → Clusters
Select a cluster (e.g., Default)
Click Permissions tab
Add cluster administrator:
User: storage_admin_01
Role: ClusterAdmin
Inherit permissions: Check this option
Subtask 2.3: Set Data Center Permissions
Navigate to Compute → Data Centers
Select the data center
Configure permissions:
User: network_admin_01
Role: DataCenterAdmin
Apply to child objects: Enable
Subtask 2.4: Configure Storage Domain Access
Navigate to Storage → Domains
Select a storage domain
Add storage-specific permissions:
# Storage domain permission example
User: storage_admin_01
Role: StorageAdmin
Resource: ISO_DOMAIN or DATA_DOMAIN
Subtask 2.5: Network Resource Permissions
Navigate to Network → Networks
Select a network
Configure network access:
User: network_admin_01
Role: NetworkAdmin
Scope: Specific network or all networks
Task 3: Test User Access Control Based on Assigned Roles
Subtask 3.1: Test VM Operator Access
Log out from the administrator account
Log in as vm_operator_01
Verify limited access:
Can view assigned virtual machines
Can start/stop/restart assigned VMs
Cannot create new VMs
Cannot access administrative functions
# Expected behavior for vm_operator_01:
# - Access to Compute → Virtual Machines (limited)
# - No access to Administration menu
# - Cannot modify cluster or host settings
Subtask 3.2: Test Storage Administrator Access
Log in as storage_admin_01
Verify storage management capabilities:
Access to Storage → Domains
Can manage storage configurations
Can view storage utilization
Limited access to other resources
Subtask 3.3: Test Network Administrator Access
Log in as network_admin_01
Test network management permissions:
Access to Network → Networks
Can create and modify networks
Can configure VLANs and network policies
Cannot access storage or host management
Subtask 3.4: Test Read-Only User Access
Log in as readonly_user_01
Verify read-only permissions:
Can view resources but cannot modify
No access to administrative functions
Cannot start/stop virtual machines
