Troubleshooting Common Issues
Issue 1: User Cannot Access Assigned Resources
Symptoms: User can log in but sees no resources

Solution:

Verify user permissions are correctly assigned
Check if permissions are inherited properly
Ensure the user is in the correct authentication domain
# Check user permissions via CLI
ovirt-engine-extensions-tool user-info --user-name=vm_operator_01
Issue 2: Role Assignment Not Taking Effect
Symptoms: User has role assigned but cannot perform expected actions

Solution:

Log out and log back in to refresh permissions
Verify role includes necessary permissions
Check for conflicting permission assignments
Issue 3: External Authentication Issues
Symptoms: External users cannot log in

Solution:

Verify authentication domain configuration
Test LDAP/AD connectivity
Check user group mappings
# Test authentication domain
engine-manage-domains validate --domain=example.com
Security Best Practices
Principle of Least Privilege
Assign minimum necessary permissions
Regularly review and audit user access
Remove unused accounts and permissions
Role Segregation
Separate administrative roles by function
Avoid assigning multiple high-privilege roles to single users
Implement approval workflows for privilege escalation
Monitoring and Auditing
Enable audit logging for user activities
Monitor permission changes
Regular access reviews and compliance checks
# Enable audit logging
engine-config -s AuditLogAgingThreshold=30
engine-config -s AuditLogCleanupTime="03:35:35"
